END_FILE tests/contract/test_code_proof_resources.py

The two outputs are `generate_code_proof_resources.py` and `tests/contract/test_code_proof_resources.py`. Tests were not run.

No unresolved contract contradiction blocked a complete candidate. Schema `pattern` values use `\A`/`\Z` so the installed Python jsonschema matcher rejects a terminal LF; that is required because an unqualified `$` would not. OID width versus `object_format`, ce1 digest identity, inventory order, and retained-byte derivation stay outside schema rejection, matching the R3 errata.
